| NTP Server 2 | time.nist.gov | Secondary NTP server |
| Update Interval | 3600 s | Update interval (1 hour) |
| Time Zone | UTC+5:30 | Time zone setting |

### SNTP Configuration
| Parameter | Value | Description |
|-----------|-------|-------------|
| Enable SNTP | Yes | Enable SNTP |
| SNTP Server | 192.168.0.1 | SNTP server IP |
| Update Interval | 60 s | Update interval |

## Network Redundancy (Optional)

### MRP (Media Redundancy Protocol)
| Parameter | Value | Description |
|-----------|-------|-------------|
| Enable MRP | No | MRP disabled (standard) |
| MRP Role | Client | MRP client role |
| Redundancy Class | A | Redundancy class |
| Recovery Time | 200 ms | Recovery time |

### PRP (Parallel Redundancy Protocol)
| Parameter | Value | Description |
|-----------|-------|-------------|
| Enable PRP | No | PRP disabled (standard) |
| PRP Role | DAN | PRP DAN role |
| Duplicate Detection | Yes | Enable duplicate detection |

## Network Performance Monitoring

### Performance Parameters
| Parameter | Target | Current | Status |
|-----------|--------|---------|--------|
| Network Load | < 50% | 15% | OK |
| Response Time | < 10 ms | 2 ms | OK |
| Error Rate | < 0.1% | 0.01% | OK |
| Availability | > 99.9% | 100% | OK |

### Bandwidth Utilization
| Application | Required | Available | Utilization |
|-------------|-----------|-----------|-------------|
| PROFINET I/O | 1 Mbps | 100 Mbps | 1% |
| HMI Communication | 0.5 Mbps | 100 Mbps | 0.5% |
| Web Server | 0.1 Mbps | 100 Mbps | 0.1% |
| SNMP/Management | 0.01 Mbps | 100 Mbps | 0.01% |
| **Total** | **1.61 Mbps** | **100 Mbps** | **1.61%** |

## Network Security Best Practices

### Physical Security
- Locate network equipment in secure area
- Use managed switches with port security
- Enable port-based access control
- Document all network connections

### Network Security
- Use separate VLAN for control network
- Implement firewall between control and office networks
- Disable unused network services
- Regular security audits

### Access Control
- Implement user authentication
- Use strong passwords
- Regular password rotation
- Log all access attempts

## Troubleshooting Network Issues

### Common Issues and Solutions
| Issue | Possible Cause | Solution |
|-------|----------------|----------|
| Cannot connect to PLC | IP address conflict | Check IP assignment |
| Slow communication | Network congestion | Check network load |
| Intermittent connection | Cable/switch issue | Check physical layer |
| HMI not updating | Update rate too slow | Adjust update rate |
| Web server inaccessible | Firewall blocking | Check firewall settings |

### Diagnostic Tools
- TIA Portal online diagnostics
- Wireshark network analysis
- Ping/Traceroute tests
- Web server diagnostic pages
- SNMP monitoring

